WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
A light ray can bend past a massive

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.200
object and still escape. General relativity connects matter

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.380
and energy with curved spacetime. The curved path

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.260
changes the direction from which we see a

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.620
background source; it does not require the source

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.160
itself to move. The rubber sheet is an

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.880
analogy, not a literal fabric pulled downward.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.750
Watch light from one background galaxy take different

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.490
paths around a foreground lens. An observer can

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:28.070
receive several apparent images, including distorted arcs. The

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.070
lens has redirected light, not created extra galaxies.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.350
A classroom photograph alone may not reveal the

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.870
exact number of distinct background sources.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.150
Near a black hole, plasma emits light while

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.970
gravity redirects or captures it. A bright ring

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.950
surrounds a shadow; it is not a solid

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.870
surface shining through the horizon. A merger also

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:51.230
changes spacetime and can send gravitational waves outward.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.730
Those waves are a different messenger from radio,

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.570
optical light or gamma rays.
